v 3
d rateshrink v0.1.1. Empirical-Bayes shrinkage for noisy small-denominator rates.
d
d Rates computed on small denominators are noisy by construction: one
d event at a five-person site can move it to the bottom of a ranking.
d rateshrink pulls each unit's raw rate toward the overall mean in
d proportion to how little data supports it, producing rates stable
d enough for dashboards, rankings, and benchmarking. Supports
d Beta-binomial shrinkage for proportions and Poisson-gamma shrinkage
d for event rates with exposure denominators, with optional posterior
d intervals and per-unit Beta-binomial reliability via rel().
d
d Companion methods paper: Field, Dong, Booth, Hastings, and Malone
d (2026, pre-print under review), "Rethinking 'Signal-To-Noise': A
d Coherent Beta-Binomial Reliability Formulation for Assessing Quality
d Measures," Far Harbor, LLC. Replication materials:
d https://github.com/ericabooth/BetaBinomialPaperMaterials
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
f rateshrink.ado
